The modules python/lplearn/core/{instance,lp,gda}.py are adapted from
lp-learner-new commit c23e6007400daae28737f91d19205233d313d043
(https://github.com/lucaslopes/lp-learner-new). The original work is by
S. R. Eshwar, Lucas Lopes Felipe, Alexandre Reiffers-Masson,
Daniel Sadoc Menasche and Gugan Thoppe, and is distributed under
GPL-3.0-or-later; see LICENSE. The legacy-only kernel helper was removed,
and the modules have moved to the lplearn namespace.

The Rust model and solver under src/model and src/solver, and src/error.rs,
are adapted from lp-learner-private commit
13529bb1235ab9a365b37689c9c30466726d5b7e, GPL-3.0-or-later. Their numerical
conventions are based on lp_learner/core/instance.py and gda.py at the Python
reference commit above. serde and serde_json are licensed MIT OR Apache-2.0.

The pie layout and palette in python/lplearn/plotting.py are adapted from
lp_learner/visualizations/policy.py and lp_learner/utils/variables/palettes.py
at the Python reference commit stated above, under GPL-3.0-or-later.

The conditional policy and fluid evaluation in python/lplearn/core/policy.py
are adapted from lp_learner/core/policy.py at the same Python reference commit,
under GPL-3.0-or-later.

The compatibility modules under python/lplearn/_legacy/ are adapted from
lp-learner-new commit c23e6007400daae28737f91d19205233d313d043 by
S. R. Eshwar, Lucas Lopes Felipe, Alexandre Reiffers-Masson,
Daniel Sadoc Menasché and Gugan Thoppe. The project is licensed under
GPL-3.0-or-later; see LICENSE. Internal imports were relocated into the
lplearn._legacy namespace. Trailing whitespace was normalized, Model now
initializes its utils dependency, and the legacy plot diagnoses invalid input.
The backup modules and experiment runner were not included in this layer.

The experiment runner and smoke stage in python/lplearn/experiments, together
with configs/smoke.toml, are adapted from the corresponding paths at the same
Python reference commit, under GPL-3.0-or-later. Imports, packaging, provenance,
Windows peak-RSS handling and pickle-free NumPy archive writing were adapted.

The aggregation, policy and saddle core modules, analysis metrics,
lp_solutions/learners experiment stages and their TOML configurations are
adapted from the corresponding Python reference paths at the commit above,
under GPL-3.0-or-later. Imports and learner non-finite checks were adapted.

The learners stage additionally dispatches to the Rust solver, records backend
identity and occupation diagnostics, and uses a new stage cache version.

The aggregation-bound analysis, experiment stage and its TOML configuration
are adapted from the corresponding Python reference paths at commit
c23e6007400daae28737f91d19205233d313d043 under GPL-3.0-or-later. Imports and
CLI examples were updated for the lplearn namespace.

The finite_n policies, mechanisms, simulator, experiment stage and TOML
configurations are adapted from the corresponding Python reference paths at
the commit above, under GPL-3.0-or-later. Imports, stage version and learned
occupation diagnostics were adapted.
